                <pb facs="0818" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4331: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-04T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1922—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 4—1:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>197. Department’s no. 108 of May 2. U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Huron</hi> is
                    due off Taku at 7 a.m tomorrow. Strauss has given orders for landing of 150
                    marines with machine guns at Tientsin by tug. U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilmington</hi> is under orders to proceed to Taku.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
